    "author_association": "NONE",
    "body": "`nvim_parse_expression()` calls `abort()` instead of returning an error when the `l` (`:let` lvalue) flag is set and the input has an unterminated `{`.\n\n```lua\nvim.api.nvim_parse_expression('{', 'l', false)\n```\n\nCommand, with the line above saved as `input.lua`:\n\n```\nnvim --headless -u NONE -i NONE -n -l input.lua\n```\n\nOn an ASan build the process dies with SIGABRT (exit 1); a release build exits 134 with no message:\n\n```\n==1172==ERROR: AddressSanitizer: ABRT on unknown address ...\n    #2 in abort\n    #3 in viml_pexpr_parse src/nvim/viml/parser/expressions.c:2133\n    #4 in nvim_parse_expression src/nvim/api/vimscript.c:470\n    #5 in nlua_api_nvim_parse_expression build/src/nvim/auto/lua_api_c_bindings.generated.h:8290\nSUMMARY: AddressSanitizer: ABRT (/lib/x86_64-linux-gnu/libc.so.6+0x969bc) in pthread_kill\n```\n\nI expected a dict with an `error` entry, not a process abort from a public API.\n\nReproduces on master at 0851e7dabed9 (ASan build: `ABRT` in `viml_pexpr_parse`; release build: exit 134, signal 6). The input came from generated tests, not from a real program.\n\nLooks like `viml_pexpr_parse` in `expressions.c`: in lvalue mode `{` creates a `kExprNodeCurlyBracesIdentifier` that is still on the AST stack at end of input, and the switch after the main loop hits `abort()` instead of setting an E15 \"Missing closing figure brace\" error.\n\nI can send a patch if that helps.\n\nFound with an LLM-based testing tool; I used Claude to reduce it and look for the cause.\n",
